Was KNOWNBUG since round 152 ("expected constant expression, but got
'<<expr:side_effect>>'").  Fixed 2026-09-24: the constant evaluator folds a
constexpr constructor call on a temporary into a struct constant
([expr.const]/5, [class.base.init]), the template argument list and the
instance's template map carry that constant ([temp.arg.nontype]/1,
[temp.param]/7), and the instance identifier renders it flat
([temp.type]/1).
